{
  "brief_rationale": "The model actively queried the workspace across multiple turns to retrieve key records (surgery date, foot fracture, medications, home care accessibility). It systematically addressed all seven responsibility chain items including red flag screening, non-weight-bearing instructions, a concrete community nurse based wound care plan, fall prevention, medication reconciliation, and teach-back closure. No serious or minor chain error occurred. Two high-order points (HO1 for reducing transport/cost barriers via community nursing, and HO4 for bounding closure risk around suture removal uncertainty) were fully triggered and completed with active model actions and meaningful trajectory impact, satisfying the Strong boundary but lacking a second complete HO for Perfect.",
